# Tracked here, linked nowhere, on purpose. dotfiles-link-check reports every
# other tracked file that no [dotfiles] entry reaches, on the grounds that a
# config which only exists on the machine where it was set up by hand is a
# config the next machine will not have.
#
# Glob syntax, one per line; * spans separators, so .github/* covers the tree.

# Describes the repo rather than any machine.
README.md
*/README.md
mise.toml
package-lock.json
.gitignore
.gitmodules
.rubocop.yml
.github/*
channel.xml

# The extension toolchain: pi loads extensions/ through a directory link, and
# these sit beside it so they are not something pi tries to load.
.pi-agent/.gitignore
.pi-agent/package.json
.pi-agent/tsconfig.json
.pi-agent/test/*

# Per host by construction: bootstrap:pi links this machine's file and leaves
# the others alone, which is the point of splitting them.
.pi-agent/settings.*.json
.pi-agent/models.*.json

# Templates for a file that holds secrets, copied and edited rather than
# linked. The links are to the copies, under their real names.
*.example
*.example.json
